              <button class="accordion-header" data-key="pure-identity">Pure Identity</button>

              <div class="accordion-content">
                <div class="accordion-inner">
                  Portraits focused on resemblance. Chosen when the goal is to preserve how your dog actually looks, including proportions, gaze and familiar expression. These styles keep intervention minimal so the result works almost like a memory, simple, calm and immediately recognizable.
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
              <button class="accordion-header" data-key="graphic-presence">Graphic Presence</button>

              <div class="accordion-content">
                <div class="accordion-inner">
                  Portraits reduced into visual language. Instead of realism the dog becomes a clear form built from shape, contour and contrast. Suitable when the image should function as a visual object rather than a sentimental piece.
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

